<title>CANADA: Canadian dollar ends firmer in quiet trading.</title>
<headline>Canadian dollar ends firmer in quiet trading.</headline>
<text>
<p>FORECAST RANGE   1.3745/1.3795	    ASIAN CLOSE     1.3752</p>
<p>RESISTANCE 1.3690   SUPPORT 1.3835	HI 1.3775   LO  1.3736</p>
<p>CANADA OPEN  1.3760/70    HI 1.3770     EUROPE OPEN     1.3757</p>
<p>PREV CLOSE   1.3762/67    LO 1.3740     HI 1.3764   LO  1.3754</p>
<p>---------------------MARKET COMMENT--------------------------</p>
<p>* Canada's dollar ended slightly firmer on Wednesday at C$1.3760 (US$0.7270) in light trading, after the unit beat back a late-morning spate of U.S. dollar buying by offshore investors, traders said. * They said the unit would likely trade in a narrow range ahead of U.S. non-farm payrolls data due on Friday.  </p>
<p>On the crosses, Canada's dollar rose to 84.46 yen from Tuesday's close of 84.29 yen and rose to 1.2556 marks from Tuesday's 1.2549 marks.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau 416 941-8100))</p>
